  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In the Expressions menu, there is a Legacy Finger option that returns the finger tracking of the Index controller to the behavior before the skeletal input update, but I would like a setting to turn this on by default.\n\nThe finger tracking range during skeletal input can be adjusted for each avatar from Unity, but this adjustment range is limited and it is not possible to make it the same range of movement as with Legacy Finger. (In addition, adjusting the range of movement affects existing hand animations, so they all have to be recreated.)\n\nEvery time you upload a new avatar, you have to enable Legacy Finger for that avatar, and sometimes even avatars that have Legacy Finger enabled can be disabled for some reason.\n\nIt would be useful to have an option to enable Legacy Finger for all avatars from the settings window in the VRChat main menu rather than for each avatar, or an option to set Legacy Finger as the default from the SDK when uploading an avatar.",
